    <!-- ── PHONE VALIDATION RULES ──────────────────────────────
         Each record defines the mobile phone format for one country:
         - digit_count: exact number of digits required (national, no +code)
         - leading_digit: set of allowed first digits. Each character is one
                          valid starting digit. "5" = must start with 5,
                          "67" = first digit must be 6 or 7.
                          Leave empty → no restriction.

         noupdate='1' → existing records are NOT overwritten on upgrade,
         so Managers can safely tweak any of these rules from the UI.
    ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->

